# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-15, from a hunt in walks of ordinary acts); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: somebody works with Safari docked on the left and pushes Mail aside by hand, low and to the left, until a corner of it
# shows: under a third, its title bar within reach. ⌃⌥⎋ to show a colleague the Mac as it is, ⌃⌥⎋ again, Quit in the evening, a
# start in the morning. At a pause and at a quit Arbor gives back what ARBOR has put out of view, and nothing else: Mail
# stays where it was left, however little of it shows, as long as somebody can get hold of it.
# Reference: F64; collab/QUESTIONS.md, Q20 and "what is found counts as left".
quiet
open Safari 1100x700 min 574x240
open Mail 1017x584
dock 101 left
move 102 -425 718 1017 584
wait 5
expect still 102

press toggle-pause
expect still 102
expect at 102 -425 718 1017x584
wait 5
expect still 102
press toggle-pause
expect docked 101
expect still 102
expect at 102 -425 718 1017x584

# Safari framed, a pause from there, and everything shown again: no view takes a floating window away (Q29, 4), so there is
# nothing of Mail's to give back, and nobody touches it.
zoom 101
expect fills 101
expect still 102
expect at 102 -425 718 1017x584
press toggle-pause
expect still 102
expect at 102 -425 718 1017x584
press toggle-pause
expect still 102
show-all
expect still 102
expect at 102 -425 718 1017x584

relaunch quit
expect at 102 -425 718 1017x584
relaunch start
expect still 102
press home
expect still 102
expect at 102 -425 718 1017x584
